pivot: complements disease_wp (sibling — reproducible burden ordering + standard-of-care survey,
       concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20763842, CC BY 4.0), turning to DNA emergence ->
       perturbation read -> treatment-direction reasoning (pathways A switch / B chemistry),
       under a structure-only firewall and a suspension rule ("no analyzable single-gene DNA -> hold").

scope: single-gene / rare / hereditary diseases (the VP_FRAMEWORK_MAP section-6 etiology-class
       contract: "disease defined by a gene" -> this track; "disease defined by dynamics" ->
       the machine/homeostasis packages). Every disease here is monogenic; common multifactorial
       forms (polygenic hypertriglyceridaemia, common obesity) are deliberately NOT in scope.
       As of v0.30.0 the kit additionally reads its MULTI-SYSTEM, INTRACTABLE (난치) subset through a
       cross-system inheritance layer (ROADMAP V): a single causal-gene lesion that manifests across
       several organ systems inherits, read-only, the REAL measured organ-master gamma of each
       affected sibling system, and the lead corrective lever's compartment REACH-vs-GAP is surfaced
       as the next treatment direction. The "major" (dynamics-defined, common/acquired) disease each
       sibling owns -- the cancers, type-2 diabetes, essential hypertension, common osteoporosis, the
       acquired sensory diseases -- remains EXCLUDED (enforced by the §6 exclusion gate).

engine:
  gamma: SantaLucia 1998 nearest-neighbour stacking dG (deterministic)
  switch: R19 cusp normal form  |h_sp| = 2*(g/3)^1.5 ;  barrier = g^2/4
  dwell:  gamma^1.5/(K+brake)  [LOCKED form]; disease/treated brakes AXIS-AWARE
          (DOWN = deficiency/over-active brake -> disease below healthy [v0.2.0 model, byte-identical];
           UP   = gain-of-toxicity/dosage-excess/released-brake-over-accumulation -> disease over-shoots;
                  corrective RESTRAINS it)
  emergence: relay-ODE gene-network (param_db.json; protein t1/2 46h, mRNA 9h, Schwanhauser 2011)
  chemistry: dG = dH - T dS @ 310.15 K ; Sabatier window ; tetrahedral 109.47 deg

