changes since v0.31.0:
  + DISEASE-ADDING release -- +4 RESOLVED, +1 SUSPENDED, NO engine change at all (every resolved lead
      reuses an EXISTING lever -- 'restrain' x2 and 'replace' x2 -> no new role / mechanism / axis /
      lever), so all 80 prior per-disease hashes stay drift 0 (80 -> 85 = 72 resolved + 13 suspended).
  + The 4 RESOLVED adds each OPEN a new molecular-corrective-axis family, each web-verified before
      shipping:
      (A) scn4a_skeletal_muscle_channelopathy (SCN4A) -- the kit's FIRST SKELETAL-MUSCLE ion channel,
          and the SKELETAL-MUSCLE TWIN of LQT3 (SCN5A): the SAME biophysics (a persistent/late sodium
          current from impaired fast inactivation) in a sister Na-channel gene and a different excitable
          tissue. Channel GOF -> membrane-excitability axis UP (myotonia; depolarisation-induced
          inexcitability) -> lead RESTRAIN with mexiletine, a class-IB Na-channel blocker that is the
          FIRST disease-specific licensed antimyotonic (NaMuscla, EMA-approved 2018 for non-dystrophic
          myotonia; phase-III MYOMEX / Statland 2012 JAMA RCT) -- and, remarkably, the SAME drug LQT3
          uses. Second INDIRECT approved arm for the paralysis variants: dichlorphenamide (Keveyis,
          FDA-approved 2015 for primary periodic paralysis), a carbonic anhydrase inhibitor acting via
          acid-base / K+, NOT on NaV1.4. Genotype-dependent magnitude [O]. SCN4A gamma 1.5187 chr17;
          axis family `skeletal_muscle_sodium_channel`; burden B2/U3/D4.
      (B) neonatal_severe_hyperparathyroidism (CASR) -- the kit's FIRST CALCIUM-SENSING-GPCR axis,
          distinct from the AVPR2 water-balance GPCR axis. The CaSR senses extracellular Ca2+ and
          SUPPRESSES PTH (a BRAKE); biallelic LOF -> NSHPT (life-threatening neonatal hypercalcaemia),
          heterozygous LOF -> FHH1 (benign). Brake released -> PTH / serum-Ca axis UP -> lead RESTRAIN
          by POTENTIATING the residual receptor with the calcimimetic cinacalcet (a DIRECT CaSR positive
          allosteric modulator). APPROVED for related hyperparathyroid conditions, used OFF-LABEL but as
          documented effective first-line therapy in NSHPT / symptomatic FHH; GENOTYPE-DEPENDENT (needs
          residual receptor; true nulls -> parathyroidectomy, a PHYSICAL fallback). Magnitude [O].
          CASR gamma 1.3299 chr3; axis family `calcium_sensing_gpcr`; burden B2/U3/D4.
      (C) biotinidase_deficiency (BTD) -- a cofactor-RECYCLING enzyme LOF: biotinidase liberates free
          biotin from biocytin during carboxylase turnover; LOF -> free-biotin pool DOWN -> the four
          biotin-dependent carboxylases under-charged (late-onset multiple carboxylase deficiency, axis
          DOWN) -> the simplest possible REPLACE: oral biotin (vitamin B7) floods the free-biotin pool
          and re-charges the carboxylases, bypassing the recycler. One of the most TREATABLE inborn
          errors (newborn-screened, inexpensive, normal course if pre-symptomatic); TIMING-limited --
          established hearing loss / optic atrophy do not reverse. Magnitude [O]. BTD gamma 1.3560 chr3;
          axis family `cofactor_recycling_replacement`; burden B2/U2/D5.
      (D) primary_carnitine_deficiency (SLC22A5 / OCTN2) -- an active carnitine-IMPORTER LOF (an
          accelerator whose drive loads cellular carnitine): LOF wastes carnitine in urine, depletes
          tissue carnitine, collapses long-chain fatty-acid oxidation (axis DOWN; hypoketotic
          hypoglycaemia, cardiomyopathy, myopathy) -> REPLACE by mass action: high-dose oral
          levocarnitine (Carnitor, FDA-approved for primary/secondary carnitine deficiency) restores
          tissue carnitine through residual uptake, REVERSING cardiomyopathy if started early. Once
          lethal, now survivable; lifelong dependence; magnitude / reversibility [O]. SLC22A5 gamma
          1.3724 chr5; axis family `carnitine_transport_replacement`; burden B2/U2/D5.
  + The SUSPEND add (charcot_marie_tooth_1a / PMP22 17p11.2 tandem duplication) is the TENTH distinct
      held MECHANISM class and the FIRST copy-number GAIN / gene-DUPLICATION-DOSAGE hold: a ~1.4-Mb
      duplication carries a THIRD complete copy of PMP22 -> over-expression by gene DOSAGE -> the
